{
  "_how_to": [
    "1. In the UE editor run: py ue_import_command_center.py --discover  -> writes ue_material_discovery.json with the game's",
    "   master materials (path + scalar / vector / texture parameter names).",
    "2. For each slot below set 'parent' to the game master material (or material instance) to use and fill 'game_param'",
    "   for every value that the master has (leave '' to skip). Values come from textures/manifest.json.",
    "3. Run: py ue_import_command_center.py --import  -> creates MI_CC_<slot> and assigns them to the mesh sections.",
    "Paint: the game master usually takes the paint-gun colours itself; then leave base_color '' on the paint slots and",
    "check U-11 (which mask the master reads: texture, vertex colour PaintMask R/G, or the slot itself).",
    "Fallback: a slot with an empty 'parent' and a 'fallback' key gets MI_CC_<slot> parented to the mod's own master (MM_CC_ScreenRT / MM_CC_Holo, built by the script); then 'fallback_param' names are used instead of 'game_param'."
  ],
